<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title>Styled HTML Page</title>
<style>
h2 {
color: blue;
font
-size: 2em;
margin
-bottom: 10px;
}
h3 {
color: pink;
font
-size: 5cm;
margin
-bottom: 8px;
}
hr {
border: 0;
height: 2px;
background
-color: red;
margin: 20px; }
p {
font
-family: "Arial";
line
-height: 1.6;
margin: 10px; }
div {
padding: 12px;
border: 3px solid black;
background
-color: pink;
color: red; }
span {
color: orange;
font
-weight: bold;
}
time {
color: green; }
img {
margin
-left: 15px;
height: 300px;
width: 400px;
border
-radius: 8px;
}
.highlighted {
background
-color: yellow;
}
a {
color: blue;
text
-decoration: underline;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h2>Main Heading</h2>
<h3>Sub Heading</h3>
<hr>
<p>This is a paragraph demonstrating the basic text styling applied by CSS.</p>
<div>
This is a styled <strong>div</strong> element with padding and a light border. Inside the div, we can also use <span>span 
element</span> that has its own styles, like this bold orange text.
</div>
<p>Current time <time>10:30 AM</time></p>
<img src="web.jpg" alt="Web Image">
<p class="highlighted">This paragraph is highlighted with a yellow background.</p>
<a href="about.html">About Us</a>
</body>
</html>
